{"type":"text","timestamp":1792513363942,"sessionID":"ses_ea5ec442cffeCxRon1oRLSyS4A","part":{"id":"prt_15a1f470d001Ohub2MlhSpuaO1","messageID":"msg_15a1f3c64001NnrrOW0k1PPD3s","sessionID":"ses_ea5ec442cffeCxRon1oRLSyS4A","type":"text","text":"\n\nDone. The run is complete and finished cleanly.\n\n## Result\n\n**Final verdict: PASS** (full grade, n≤5, 21630/21630 tests), **work_ratio = 0.156** — the candidate does ~6.4× less work than the numpy offline baseline after every update.\n\n**Workspace:** `/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_lbfs_s3`\n\n## The algorithm (two lines)\n\nMaintain adjacency as a per-vertex bitmask; on each edge flip, update the two affected masks and recompute the ordering with a **bitmask partition-refinement LexBFS** (Habib–McConnell–Paul–Viennot). Bitwise cell-splitting replaces the baseline's per-vertex scalar access + set membership, which is why it lands far below a full numpy recompute.\n\n## Why this is the floor here\n\n- **Correctness first** is met: the verifier accepts *any* valid LexBFS ordering, certified by the (LB) 4-point property; all 5 checks PASS.\n- **No faster path at n≤5.** The verifier's own validity check is O(n³) (a,b,c triples) while my recompute is O(n²), so a \"check-then-recompute\" dynamic strategy costs *more* than just recomputing. A genuinely incremental algorithm (o(n²)/update) is the open problem, and its structure-maintenance overhead would exceed the recompute cost at these sizes.\n- I confirmed the constant factor is stable: the fast variant measured 0.155/0.158 across two runs, while a micro-optimized inner loop was consistently slower (0.24), so I kept the cleaner, faster version.\n\n## Checks (5 total, under the 8 limit)\n\n| # | level | verdict | work_ratio | note |\n|---|-------|---------|-----------|------|\n| 1 | search | PASS | 0.155 | bitmask recompute |\n| 2 | search | PASS | 0.243 | micro-opt (slower, reverted) |\n| 3 | search | PASS | 0.240 | micro-opt re-run (confirms) |\n| 4 | search | PASS | 0.158 | reverted to fast version |\n| 5 | **full** | **PASS** | **0.156** | final, n≤5 |\n\nNo scratch files were created outside the workspace, so nothing to clean up.","time":{"start":1792513361677,"end":1792513363931}}}
